WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.160
We started football on the . . . say the first of September and of course we played all the way up to the Sugar [Bowl] . . . first of January for the last two years [1935-1936],

2
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:19.380
then it was all over till we start spring training in February and then, ain’t no limit on spring training.

3
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.740
Hell, you’d play till Bernie Moore got tired of scrimmaging.

4
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.940
And we would scrimmage during the regular season three and four days a week.

5
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:34.820
So, I always had to get out early to work with the punters and the receivers, as I say, being a center.

6
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.680
That’s about the extent of my football at LSU.

7
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.533
And as I say, I was fortunate enough to make two or three Southeastern Conference and All-American teams.
